  "notes": "Wu (Shanghainese, Suzhounese, …) romanised input contract: Wugniu (吳語學堂 scheme), built on Qian Nairong's 2007 Shanghainese phonology. Wu is distinctive for a three-way stop/affricate voicing contrast (voiceless unaspirated / voiceless aspirated / voiced, e.g. p/ph/b), each series a separate cited grapheme (test 2: one laryngeal-setting segment per letter). gn spells the palatal nasal /ɲ/ (test 1: not derivable from g+n, which the language spells differently). Wu tone is lexical with pervasive tone sandhi across whole prosodic words that this skeleton does not yet encode (a sandhi_rules gap, not a stress gap: the stress schema itself does not apply, tonal-language exemption per quality_tiers.md). No WikiPron gold exists in this romanisation (WikiPron's wuu_hani file is Han-character keyed), so the tier stays at skeleton.",
